    },
    {
      "start": 83.96,
      "end": 87.14,
      "text": "they call it limit like it's clean and defined"
    },
    {
      "start": 87.14,
      "end": 90.46,
      "text": "but it feels like losing my mind"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.4,
      "end": 104.86,
      "text": "every voice says you're not enough but dresses it in polished stuff"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.86,
      "end": 110.32,
      "text": "equations i don't understand still somehow written in my hands"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.32,
      "end": 115.36,
      "text": "a bright white heart compressed and tight holding out against the night"
    },
    {
      "start": 115.36,
      "end": 120.9,
      "text": "but every doubt i try to hide adds another layer deep inside"
    },
    {
      "start": 120.9,
      "end": 131.84,
      "text": "i'm still standing but i bend a fragile state of outward calm"
    },
    {
      "start": 131.84,
      "end": 141.22,
      "text": "while everything leans toward the dawn am i past the point where i can hold this form"
    },
    {
      "start": 142.3,
      "end": 150.24,
      "text": "where the pressure builds and the self deforms if i cross that line do i disappear"
    },
    {
      "start": 150.24,
      "end": 154.4,
      "text": "or collapse into something more severe they call it limit"
    },
    {
      "start": 154.4,
